**Step 3. Checks per object, printed with a control, BEFORE any removal** (a failed check HOLDS that object only; nothing is worked around): (1) exists (`ls -d`; absent: record ABSENT); (2) its lane's pull request merged (Step 2); (3) clause 3: `date -v-3d` cutoff taken at that command; `find <path> -newermt "<cutoff>" -print -quit` prints nothing AND `stat` of the path is older (control: `find` on your own `.tools/b1300` prints a file); (4) not held: `ps -axo command` holds no line with the path or tag (control: your own `ps` line matches a planted word), `lsof -nP -- /tmp/x_never` empty (control: a file you hold open lists), `docker ps -a --filter ancestor=<tag>` empty; (5) each tree registered (`.git/worktrees/<name>/gitdir` names it) AND clean (`git --no-optional-locks -C '<tree>' status --porcelain` empty; control: a scratch dir with an untracked file prints it) else HOLD; (6) `/usr/bin/grep -n -F` of the object's path in the project's `Briefs/*_STATUS.md` and in non-`.pre-` kits: a STATUS naming a file inside it as where a figure lives = HOLD that directory (the lines that merely list it as owed are not such a naming: print and classify each hit).
**Step 4. Locks and load.** seat-local lock `.tools/b1300/removal.lock` by `mkdir` (exists: STOP); load1 under 7 on two reads 2 minutes apart, waiting at most 15 minutes, then defer. A heartbeat loop writes `date` every 30 s into `.tools/b1300/hb/heartbeat.txt` while a removal command runs; two reads 35 s apart must differ.
**Step 5. Remove** (one object per command, `ls -d` before and after, rc printed): registered trees by `git --no-optional-locks -C '<Root>/2_Project_Files' worktree remove '<exact tree>'` (no `--force`; a refusal is HOLD); directories by `rm -r -- '<exact path>'` (after Step 3 passes for it); images by `docker image rm '<exact name:tag>'` (an in-use refusal is HOLD); the file by `rm -- '/tmp/x_never'`. **Docker only for `image ls`, `image inspect`, `ps -a --filter`, `system df` and `image rm` of the five tags of List A.** An unregistered tree (`wt-b1085-merge`, Q-3) is NOT removed by `rm -r` unless the Stamp says `REMOVE-UNREGISTERED: YES`; by default it is MOVED to `.tools/b1300/quarantine/` and named. A hook refusal: report, stop that object, do not route around. Order: List A trees, List A directories (`b1084`, `b1047`, `b1101`), then List B, then images, then the file.
**Step 6. Count and measure.** After each class: objects present per class before and after, `du -sk` of each remaining path, `df -k` avail (re-read after 60 s), `docker image ls` rows, `docker system df`; print removed, held, absent, moved, and the free-space difference by program (expected about 2.0 GiB plus the images; if the difference is under half of that, say so, do not explain it away). Release the lock by `mv` into `.tools/b1300/quarantine/`. Confirm untouched by program: `ls -d` of every NEVER path, `git --no-optional-locks -C '<Root>' status --porcelain` not changed in any tracked path by this seat.
