- **Partition:** this seat writes nothing that another seat writes; it removes only what the property names. Another seat's lane (B1108's trees, B1123's tree, any `_wt_*`) is read only. If a tree turns out to be live (a pane, a process, a file touched after the cutoff): HOLD it, never wait it out and never `--force`.
- Never print a credential. No `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (the Root has spaces and an `!`); `/usr/bin/grep`; every count with a positive control that can fail.
